Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage for this task  

• event_name → filter only real purchase events (`'purchase'`).  
• event_date  → restrict to December‑2020 tables / rows (`'20201201'–'20201231'`).  
• ecommerce.transaction_id → lets us group all items that belong to the same order.  
• items (repeated record)  
  – items.item_name       → identify “Google Navy Speckled Tee” and every other product.  
  – items.quantity        → measure how many units of each product were bought.  
• user_pseudo_id → alternative key in case you want to study the same user across several orders.  
• _TABLE_SUFFIX (virtual)  → helps you query every daily table whose name starts with `events_202012`.  

Typical conditions you will need  
• WHERE event_name = 'purchase'  
• AND _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '202012%'  
• AND LOWER(items.item_name) LIKE '%google%navy%speckled%tee%'  

Below are ten exploratory BigQuery queries (each limited to 20 rows) that go from very simple inspections to the final aggregation that returns “the other product with the highest total quantity purchased together with the Google Navy Speckled Tee in December 2020”.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a single December day to see the structure of purchase events
SELECT event_date,
       event_timestamp,
       event_name,
       ecommerce.transaction_id,
       items
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201228`
WHERE  event_name = 'purchase'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List distinct item names that contain the words “speckled” and “tee” to be sure of the exact spelling
SELECT DISTINCT items.item_name
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201228`,
       UNNEST(items) AS items
WHERE  LOWER(items.item_name) LIKE '%speckled%tee%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Get 20 purchase rows (any December day) that include the Google Navy Speckled Tee
SELECT _TABLE_SUFFIX        AS event_table,
       ecommerce.transaction_id,
       event_timestamp,
       items.item_name,
       items.quantity
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
       UNNEST(items) AS items
WHERE  _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '202012%'
  AND  event_name        = 'purchase'
  AND  LOWER(items.item_name) LIKE '%google%navy%speckled%tee%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Inspect every other item that appears in the *same* transaction as the tee (single day example)
SELECT e.ecommerce.transaction_id,
